> # The ONE ports entry allowed here is the command channel's, and only because
> # the base file does not bind it. Compose CONCATENATES ports lists across files,
> # so publishing a port the base already has would add a SECOND binding rather
> # than replace it, and the second container to start would fail to bind — after
> # the build, not before it. 7878 has no base binding on this family, so there is
> # nothing for it to be appended to. `test_composegen.py` fails the build if any
> # other port appears here.
